hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1598","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated to us, al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was... He raised his head from bowing and did not stop standing until we saw him prostrating.\""
1599"""
"1599","'Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Maslamah ibn Salih narrated to us — and there is something in the heart regarding him — from al-Walid ibn Sari', from 'Amr ibn Hurayth, who said: ""I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he raised his head from bowing, none of us would bend his back until we saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had prostrated."""
